  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129499/assets/3d3f0d6f8d39e9f34ef831a83120257c2961708f6cb7daf87a35a1a9a750441d.png)\n\nEach of the two shapes in the model above represents one whole. Insert the missing numbers in the division problem below.\n\n{{field-1}}\n$÷\\,\\frac{1}{4}=$\n{{field-2}}",
  "worked_solution": "In the model, there are $2$ shapes. Each shape consists of $4$ pieces that each represent $\\frac{1}{4}$ of a whole. There are $8$ pieces in total.\n\nThe model tells us that when we divide $2$ wholes into quarters, we will be left with $8$ pieces.\n\nHence, the division problem is\n\n$$\n2÷\\frac{1}{4}=8.\n$$",
